msgid ":mod:`!html.entities` --- Definitions of HTML general entities"
msgstr ":mod:`!html.entities` --- definitioner av generella HTML-entiteter"

msgid "**Source code:** :source:`Lib/html/entities.py`"
msgstr "**Källkod:** :source:`Lib/html/entities.py`"

msgid ""
"This module defines four dictionaries, :data:`html5`, "
":data:`name2codepoint`, :data:`codepoint2name`, and :data:`entitydefs`."
msgstr ""
"Modulen definierar fyra ordböcker: :data:`html5`, :data:`name2codepoint`, "
":data:`codepoint2name` och :data:`entitydefs`."

msgid ""
"A dictionary that maps HTML5 named character references [#]_ to the "
"equivalent Unicode character(s), e.g. ``html5['gt;'] == '>'``. Note that the"
" trailing semicolon is included in the name (e.g. ``'gt;'``), however some "
"of the names are accepted by the standard even without the semicolon: in "
"this case the name is present with and without the ``';'``. See also "
":func:`html.unescape`."
msgstr ""
"En ordbok som mappar namngivna HTML5-teckenreferenser [#]_ till motsvarande "
"Unicode-tecken, till exempel ``html5['gt;'] == '>'``. Observera att det "
"avslutande semikolonet ingår i namnet, till exempel ``'gt;'``. Vissa namn "
"godtas dock av standarden även utan semikolon. I det fallet finns namnet "
"både med och utan ``';'``. Se även :func:`html.unescape`."

msgid ""
"A dictionary mapping XHTML 1.0 entity definitions to their replacement text "
"in ISO Latin-1."
msgstr ""
"En ordbok som mappar XHTML 1.0-entitetsdefinitioner till deras "
"ersättningstext i ISO Latin-1."

msgid "A dictionary that maps HTML4 entity names to the Unicode code points."
msgstr "En ordbok som mappar HTML4-entitetsnamn till Unicode-kodpunkterna."

msgid "A dictionary that maps Unicode code points to HTML4 entity names."
msgstr "En ordbok som mappar Unicode-kodpunkter till HTML4-entitetsnamn."

msgid "Footnotes"
msgstr "Fotnoter"

msgid ""
"See https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/named-characters.html#named-"
"character-references"
msgstr ""
"Se https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/named-characters.html#named-"
"character-references"
